kkrueg@ukelele.GCR.COM (Karl Krueger) writes:
: simpsong@sun1.bham.ac.uk (Glyn Simpson) writes:
: 
: >S J Arnott (geas@castle.ed.ac.uk) wrote:
: >> A simple disscuion question.
: 
: >> If you were a lowish level character and be some means or other you got
: >> yourself a wish.......
: 
: >> WHAT WOULD YOU WISH FOR?
: 
: >I would normally go for a decent weapon, Vorpal Blade, Excalibur or Stormy
: 
: First choice:  aligned weapon (Exc., VB, S, Mj., Tsurugi of Myamasa, or as
: appropriate for class/alignment)
: 
Yup me too.

: Second choice:  GDSM
: 
Probably.

: Third choice:  Blessed bag of holding
:
Not I, these are fairly common later on...  If you want carrying power get
gauntlets of power!
 
: Fourth choice:  Blessed shield of reflection
: 
Yes yes yes.  Or an amulet if ya have a 2-H weapon.  Reflection is fairly
vital with all those darn gnomes with wands of fire (etc.)

: Fifth choice:  Blessed luckstone
:
Again, I wouldn't ever waste a wish on one.  Too common in 3.1.
 
: Sixth choice:  Wand of digging
:
What, are you high? :)  Kill a minotaur.  If you want to rob a shop, there
are better ways too...  Although digging can be a good quick escape device.
 
: Seventh choice:  Amulet of life saving
:
Good to have one or two whenever possible!
 
: Etc.  Etc.  Etc.
:
Speaking of etc:
	(1) A blessed ring of teleport control
		With intrinsic teleport, you have a means of quick escape
		and instant travel!  Also a quick way to escape being
		swallowed, death by drowning (if lucky), and a great way to
		un-satiate yourself very quickly for intrinsic gaining.
	(2) A blessed ring of conflict
		Never again be gang-banged by hordes of angry monsters.
		Let them chop each other up for you!  Use with caution, and
		remove before the Astral Plane!!!
	(3) A blessed +3 pair of speed boots
		MAKE THIS YOUR FIRST WISH!  If you've wasted your first,
		MAKE THIS YOUR SECOND WISH!  These are ABSOLUTELY THE BEST
		ITEM IN THE GAME HANDS DOWN NO COMPETITION.  Period.
	(4) Miscellaneous armors
		a blessed +3 cloak of displacement (and make yourself invis)
		a blessed +3 helm of telepathy (or brilliance if stupid)
		a blessed +3 Hawaiian shirt (wear under armor)
		a blessed +3 gauntlets of power (or dex if strong/clumsy)
	(5) A blessed ring of levitation
		If you do not have an uncursed levitation device, let me
		assure you that it becomes fairly vital during the endgame.
		Besides, it's handy for crossing moats, swamps, lava pits,
		those pits in the castle...
	(6) 3 blessed scrolls of charging (or 2)
		Yes, recharge those lamps and wands after ya use em up.
		And then don't forget about that last wish you can squeeze
		out of em...
	(7) 3 blessed scrolls of remove curse
		If you have all the eq you need, try planting one of these
		at safe areas...  Comes in real handy when the wiz and hell
		itself have reduced your equipment to a pile of cursed
		junk!  Keep em in a bag, or fire/cursing will do them in...
	(8) 3 blessed scrolls of gold detection
		I know what you're thinking... how many drugs did this guy
		do before posting?  There is an excellent reason for this
		wish however.  First, confuse yourself.  Next, read one of
		these babies.  See all the traps appear before your eyes?
		This is _REALLY_ a lifesaver when you're looking for those
		hidden magic portals in the endgame!!!  Just use your
		cursor to ID all the traps, and you'll find the portal in
		one move.  Then teleport on top of it and VOOM!  Just don't
		let the gold detection scroll become cursed, or they
		become much less useful...

Well, that's all the wishing wisdom that comes to mind right now.

